OHOS: make fspy_preload_unix build (vite-task, applied to the vite-task-src resource).

fspy tracks file accesses through the LD_PRELOAD library fspy_preload_unix,
which fspy reaches through a -Z bindeps artifact dependency. Two things in it
do not build on OHOS:

- libc::statx and execveat do not exist in OHOS's libc, so those two
  interceptions are gated out (a libuv statx still goes through the
  intercepted syscall()).
- the variadic exec* interceptions need the c_variadic feature, which is
  stable on upstream's pinned nightly but not on the stable toolchain built
  with RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1.

Only fspy_preload_unix is touched. Re-generate it against the new vite-task
revision whenever the vite-task-src resource moves.

